# Echo Ledger — project rules

## What we build
An agent that watches up to 20 crypto KOLs, detects independent narrative
convergence (penalising echo / quote-chains), checks market evidence
(did the narrative lead or chase price), runs a Bull/Bear/Judge debate, and
opens PRACTICE (paper) positions only. Every decision produces a
"reasoning card" (JSON). Chainlink CRE workflows fetch consensus prices,
enforce a deterministic risk gate, write the position + card hash to an
EchoLedger contract on Ethereum Sepolia, settle positions, and update KOL trust.
Hackathon: BLI Legal Tech Hackathon 2 — bounties RYO-CHAN Autonomous Agents
and Chainlink "Best workflow with CRE". Deadline 2026-10-31.

## Layout
- shared/     ReasoningCard schema (zod + JSON Schema), canonical hash, types
- contracts/  Foundry, Solidity ^0.8.24, EchoLedger.sol (CRE consumer)
- cre/        CRE project (TypeScript SDK, Bun): workflows record, settle, reputation
- agent/      TypeScript + Bun: ingest, extract (LLM), converge, evidence, debate, card, replay
- dashboard/  Vite + React + TypeScript + viem, dark UI
- fixtures/   recorded KOL posts + prices for deterministic replay/demo

## Dev environment
- Windows 11 + Windows PowerShell 5.1. Write helper scripts as .ps1, use Windows paths.
- No bash-only syntax in commands you give me: no &&, export, mkdir -p, \ line continuation.
- Foundry binaries live in %USERPROFILE%\.foundry\bin (already on PATH).

## Hard rules
- NEVER read, print or commit .env files or private keys. Use .env.example with placeholders.
- NEVER deploy to mainnet. Testnet only, and ask me before any command that
  sends a transaction (forge script --broadcast, cre ... --broadcast).
- PRACTICE trading only. No real orders, no exchange keys.
- LLM output is never trusted inside CRE. LLM runs in agent/; CRE logic is deterministic.
- For anything CRE: read the official docs FIRST (links below), quote the API you use,
  and verify with `cre workflow simulate` before saying it works.
- Keep the ReasoningCard schema in shared/ as the single source of truth.
- Small steps: after each step run the relevant test/build and show me the result.
- Write clear commit messages; do not commit unless I ask.

